{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.rescaled_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.rescaled_pair","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.lean#L95-L108","doc":"The pseudo-reflection pair `{1, e^{2πiμ}}`, rescaled by `c` so that the product is `−1`,\nis the Hecke pair `{±q, ∓q⁻¹}`: `c² = q⁻²` and `(c·e^{2πiμ})² = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.not_exp_eq_neg_sq_of_im_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.not_exp_eq_neg_sq_of_im_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.lean#L89-L93","doc":"Refutation form: a **real** exponent never gives the Hecke ratio. Scope-(b), invariant =\nthe modulus of the monodromy eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.im_ne_zero_of_exp_eq_neg_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.im_ne_zero_of_exp_eq_neg_sq","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.lean#L76-L87","doc":"**The twist exponent is never real.** For real `q > 1`, `e^{2πiμ} = −q²` forces\n`Im μ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.im_eq_of_exp_eq_neg_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.im_eq_of_exp_eq_neg_sq","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.lean#L60-L74","doc":"**The exponent's imaginary part is the level.** If `e^{2πiμ} = −q²` with real `q > 0`,\nthen `Im μ = −ln q / π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.norm_exp_two_pi_I_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.norm_exp_two_pi_I_mul","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TwistedPeriodEigenvalueRatio.lean#L53-L58","doc":"`‖e^{2πiμ}‖ = e^{−2π·Im μ}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}